snapshot[23763-35649 of 796688]:
    @.900 text ". The Moon was volcanically active until 1.2 billion years ago, surfacing lava mostly on the thinner near side of the Moon, filling ancient craters, which through cooling formed the today prominently visible dark plains of "
    @.901 link "basalt" description="Basalt" url="/wiki/Basalt"
    @.903 text " called "
    @.904 link "maria" description="Lunar mare" url="/wiki/Lunar_mare"
    @.906 text " ('seas'). The "
    @.907 link "origin of the Moon" description="Origin of the Moon" url="/wiki/Origin_of_the_Moon"
    @.909 text " is not clear, although it is thought to have been formed out of material from Earth that was ejected by "
    @.910 link "a giant impact" description="Giant-impact hypothesis" url="/wiki/Giant-impact_hypothesis"
    @.912 text " of a "
    @.913 link "Mars-sized body" description="Theia (planet)" url="/wiki/Theia_(planet)"
    @.915 text " 4.51billion years ago, not long after "
    @.918 link "Earth's formation" description="Age of Earth" url="/wiki/Age_of_Earth"
    @.920 text ".From a distance, the day and night phases of the lunar day are visible as the "
    @.922 link "lunar phases" description="Lunar phases" url="/wiki/Lunar_phases"
    @.924 text ", and when the Moon passes through "
    @.925 link "Earth's shadow" url="/wiki/Earth's_shadow"
    @.927 text " a "
    @.928 link "lunar eclipse" description="Lunar eclipse" url="/wiki/Lunar_eclipse"
    @.930 text " is observable. The Moon's "
    @.931 link "apparent size" description="Apparent size" url="/wiki/Apparent_size"
    @.933 text " in Earth's sky is about the same as that of the Sun, which causes it to cover the Sun completely during a total "
    @.934 link "solar eclipse" description="Solar eclipse" url="/wiki/Solar_eclipse"
    @.936 text ". The Moon is the "
    @.937 link "brightest celestial object" description="List of brightest natural objects in the sky" url="/wiki/List_of_brightest_natural_objects_in_the_sky"
    @.939 text " in Earth's "
    @.940 link "night sky" description="Night sky" url="/wiki/Night_sky"
    @.942 text " because of its large apparent size, while the "
    @.943 link "reflectance" description="Reflectance" url="/wiki/Reflectance"
    @.945 text " (albedo) of its surface is comparable to that of "
    @.946 link "asphalt" description="Asphalt concrete" url="/wiki/Asphalt_concrete"
    @.948 text ". About 59% of the surface of the Moon is visible from Earth owing to the different angles at which the Moon can appear in Earth's sky ("
    @.949 link "libration" description="Libration" url="/wiki/Libration"
    @.951 text "), making parts of the "
    @.952 link "far side of the Moon" description="Far side of the Moon" url="/wiki/Far_side_of_the_Moon"
    @.954 text " visible.The Moon has been an important source of inspiration and knowledge in human history, having been crucial to "
    @.956 link "cosmography" description="Cosmography" url="/wiki/Cosmography"
    @.958 text ", "
    @.959 link "mythology" description="Mythology" url="/wiki/Mythology"
    @.961 text ", "
    @.962 link "religion" description="Lunar deity" url="/wiki/Lunar_deity"
    @.964 text ", art, "
    @.965 link "time keeping" description="Lunar calendar" url="/wiki/Lunar_calendar"
    @.967 text ", "
    @.968 link "natural science" description="Natural science" url="/wiki/Natural_science"
    @.970 text " and "
    @.971 link "spaceflight" description="Spaceflight" url="/wiki/Spaceflight"
    @.973 text ". The "
    @.974 link "first spaceflights" description="Timeline of Solar System exploration" url="/wiki/Timeline_of_Solar_System_exploration"
    @.976 text " to an extraterrestrial body were to the Moon, starting in 1959 with the "
